<title>USA: San Francisco tobacco suit dismissed.</title>
<headline>San Francisco tobacco suit dismissed.</headline>
<dateline>OAKLAND, Calif. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A federal judge has dismissed a lawsuit filed by the City and County of San Francisco and 10 other California counties against the tobacco industry, according to court papers made public Thursday.</p>
<p>The ruling, dated Wednesday, was issued by U.S. District Judge D. Lowell Jensen in the U.S. District Court in the Northern District of California in Oakland. Although the judge dismissed the suit, he ruled that the plaintiffs lawyers could refile an amended complaint.</p>
</text>
